{
  "description": "Attachment verb rules. Each case runs `code` as Python with the five verbs `attach`, `list_attachments`, `get_attachment`, `read_attachment` and `show_attachment` in an empty store. The code needs bytes only, or the directory `.`, and puts the result in `out`. `expect` is the answer of the engine. For a value, `json` holds the fields of `out` that the case fixes, and `keys` holds each key of `out`. For a refusal, `error` is the class name and `message` is its text. The engine test `door-parity-test` runs each case in `python_execution`, in a sandbox worker and in a real extension worker. The SDK test `test_attach_parity.py` runs each case on the host outside Vis. Where that host answers differently, the case has an `outside` object with a `reason` (a key of `exceptions`) and its own `expect`.",
  "exceptions": {
    "audience": "Outside Vis, no rule keeps a document for the user only. The audience is the one that the call names, else `both`.",
    "position": "Outside Vis, the descriptor that a read verb returns has no `position` key.",
    "error-class": "In Vis, a refusal of the engine is `VisToolError`, a `RuntimeError`. Outside Vis that class does not exist: the refusal is a `RuntimeError` with the same words.",
    "bytes": "Outside Vis, the bytes of a payload do not name its media type or its kind. The filename and the call name them."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "attach-bytes",
      "code": [
        "out = attach(b'a,b\\n1,2\\n', 'totals.csv', label='Totals')"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "json": {
          "audience": "user",
          "filename": "totals.csv",
          "is_pending": true,
          "kind": "file",
          "media_type": "text/csv",
          "size": 8,
          "source": "tool",
          "version": 1
        },
        "keys": [
          "audience",
          "filename",
          "id",
          "is_pending",
          "kind",
          "media_type",
          "size",
          "source",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "outside": {
        "reason": "audience",
        "expect": {
          "json": {
            "audience": "both",
            "filename": "totals.csv",
            "is_pending": true,
            "kind": "file",
            "media_type": "text/csv",
            "size": 8,
            "source": "tool",
            "version": 1
          },
          "keys": [
            "audience",
            "filename",
            "id",
            "is_pending",
            "kind",
            "media_type",
            "size",
            "source",
            "version"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "attach-kind",
      "code": [
        "out = attach(b'words\\n', 'w.txt', kind='note')"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "json": {
          "audience": "both",
          "kind": "note",
          "media_type": "text/plain"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "attach-kind-positional",
      "code": [
        "out = attach(b'words\\n', 'w.txt', 'note', 'text/x-note', 'Cap', 'user')"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "json": {
          "audience": "user",
          "kind": "note",
          "media_type": "text/x-note"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "attach-media-type-number",
      "code": [
        "out = attach(b'x\\n', 'n.bin', media_type=5)"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "json": {
          "kind": "file",
          "media_type": "5"
        }
      }
    },
